        "\n",
        "This is a complete vector-space retrieval system in a few lines of NumPy.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Term weighting as diagonal scaling\n",
        "\n",
        "Raw count matrices are often not the best representation.  Common words may dominate similarity.  TF-IDF corrects this by increasing the weight of terms that are frequent in a document but rare across the corpus.\n",
        "\n",
        "Let\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{tf}_{ij}=X_{ij}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "or a transformed frequency such as $\\log(1+X_{ij})$.  The document frequency of term $j$ is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{df}_j=\\#\\{i:X_{ij}>0\\}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "A smoothed inverse document frequency is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{idf}_j=\\log\\left(\\frac{1+n}{1+\\operatorname{df}_j}\\right)+1.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Then\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "X^{\\operatorname{tfidf}}_{ij}=\\operatorname{tf}_{ij}\\operatorname{idf}_j.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "In matrix form, this is column scaling:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "X^{\\operatorname{tfidf}}=XW,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "W=\\operatorname{diag}(\\operatorname{idf}_1,\\ldots,\\operatorname{idf}_d).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Thus TF-IDF is not just a heuristic.  It is a diagonal linear transformation of the feature space."
      ],
