        "## Low-rank retrieval\n",
        "\n",
        "In raw vector-space retrieval, the query score is computed in the original vocabulary space:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "s=Xq.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "In LSA retrieval, we first project the query into the latent right-singular-vector space:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "z_q=q^TV_k.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The document coordinates are\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "Z=XV_k=U_k\\Sigma_k.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Then the latent retrieval score is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "s_i=z_i^Tz_q.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "In matrix form,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "s=Zz_q^T.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "If cosine similarity is desired, normalize the latent document coordinates and the latent query coordinate before scoring."
