        "\n",
        "Ask an AI tool to predict which query will fail and why.  Then test the prediction using Python.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Common mistakes\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Confusing documents and terms.**  If $X\\in R^{n\\times d}$, rows are documents and columns are terms.  Some books use the transpose convention, so always check the orientation.\n",
        "2. **Using raw inner products without thinking about length.**  Long documents can dominate raw scores.\n",
        "3. **Calling SVD topics probabilities.**  SVD factors are real-valued and may be negative.  They are not probability distributions.\n",
        "4. **Assuming low-rank always improves retrieval.**  Low-rank projection can remove noise, but it can also remove important rare information.\n",
        "5. **Overinterpreting two-dimensional plots.**  A 2D map may be useful for visualization but may not preserve all relevant distances.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Exercises\n",
        "\n",
